.TH SVERB 1 "" "sverb 1.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sverb \- SSH client and server manager for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsverb\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
sverb is a terminal\-native SSH client and server manager. Running it without a command opens the TUI: hosts, groups, identities, keys, port forwards, snippets, workspaces, tabs and split panes, all kept in an encrypted local vault. Sync between devices, team vaults and terminal sharing need a self\-hosted sverb\-server and are optional; everything else works offline. The headless commands below manage the same vault from scripts; those that need it unlocked prompt for the master password on the terminal or use the OS keyring.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Log at debug level and keep recent log lines for the log pane (log files may then contain hostnames)
.TP
\fB\-\-workspace\fR \fINAME\fR
Launch the TUI and open this workspace
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see more with '\-\-help')
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "sverb connect"
\fBsverb connect\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fITARGET\fR
.PP
Launch the TUI with a session open (fuzzy host match or user@host:port)
.TP
\fITARGET\fR
A host label, address or fuzzy match, or `user@host:port`
.SS "sverb hosts"
\fBsverb hosts\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR
.PP
List, add and remove hosts
.SS "sverb hosts list"
\fBsverb hosts list\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
List hosts
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON (`{"version":1,"data":\[u2026]}`)
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fITAG\fR
Only hosts with this tag (repeatable; all must match)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
Only hosts in this group
.SS "sverb hosts add"
\fBsverb hosts add\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIADDRESS\fR
.PP
Add a host
.TP
\fIADDRESS\fR
Hostname or IP address
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fILABEL\fR
Display label (defaults to the address)
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fIUSER\fR
Login user
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR
SSH port
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
Group to put the host in (must exist unless \-\-create\-group)
.TP
\fB\-\-create\-group\fR
Create the group if it does not exist
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fITAG\fR
Tag (repeatable; missing tags are created)
.SS "sverb hosts rm"
\fBsverb hosts rm\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIHOST\fR
.PP
Remove a host
.TP
\fIHOST\fR
Label, address or unique fuzzy match
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Do not ask for confirmation (required without a terminal)
.SS "sverb keys"
\fBsverb keys\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.PP
Manage SSH keys, or print the effective keymap with \-\-dump
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\fR
Print the effective keymap (built\-ins and config overrides)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
With \-\-dump: print JSON (`{"version":1,"data":\[u2026]}`)
.SS "sverb keys list"
\fBsverb keys list\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
List keys in the vault (no private material)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON (`{"version":1,"data":\[u2026]}`)
.SS "sverb keys generate"
\fBsverb keys generate\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Generate a key
.TP
\fB\-\-type\fR \fIKEY_TYPE\fR
Key algorithm [possible values: ed25519, ecdsa\-p256, ecdsa\-p384, ecdsa\-p521, rsa\-2048, rsa\-3072, rsa\-4096]
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fILABEL\fR
Label for the key
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fICOMMENT\fR
Key comment (default `user@hostname\-sverb`)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-passphrase\fR
Do not ask for a passphrase (scripts)
.SS "sverb keys import"
\fBsverb keys import\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR
.PP
Import a key file (OpenSSH, PEM, PKCS#8, or a .pub agent / hardware key)
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
The key file
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fILABEL\fR
Label for the key (default: its comment, else the file name)
.SS "sverb keys export"
\fBsverb keys export\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Export a key
.TP
\fIKEY\fR
Key label or id
.TP
\fB\-\-public\fR
Export only the public key
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
Write to this file (private keys: mode 0600)
.SS "sverb forward"
\fBsverb forward\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIRULE\fR
.PP
Run a port\-forward rule headless
.TP
\fIRULE\fR
Port\-forward rule name or id
.TP
\fB\-\-detach\fR
Keep running in the background
.SS "sverb snippet"
\fBsverb snippet\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR
.PP
Run snippets on hosts
.SS "sverb snippet run"
\fBsverb snippet run\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fISNIPPET\fR
.PP
Run a snippet on one or more hosts
.TP
\fISNIPPET\fR
Snippet name or id
.TP
\fB\-\-on\fR \fIHOST|#TAG|GROUP\fR
Target: a host, `#tag` or group (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON (`{"version":1,"data":\[u2026]}`)
.TP
\fB\-\-var\fR \fINAME=VALUE\fR
A variable value, `name=value` (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-concurrency\fR \fICONCURRENCY\fR
Hosts worked on at once (default 10)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIS\fR
Seconds per command (default `ssh.exec_timeout_secs`)
.SS "sverb import"
\fBsverb import\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR
.PP
Import hosts, keys and settings
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be imported without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fIVAULT\fR
Vault to import into (default: Personal)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
Group to import into (a name or a path like a/b; default: the top level)
.TP
\fB\-\-on\-conflict\fR \fION_CONFLICT\fR
What to do with items that already exist with other values [possible values: skip, overwrite, keep\-both]
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Import without asking (required without a terminal)
.TP
\fB\-\-identity\-files\fR
Also import the IdentityFiles of an ssh_config as keys
.SS "sverb import ssh\-config"
\fBsverb import ssh\-config\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.PP
Hosts from an OpenSSH config (default ~/.ssh/config)
.TP
\fIPATH\fR
Path to the config file
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be imported without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fIVAULT\fR
Vault to import into (default: Personal)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
Group to import into (a name or a path like a/b; default: the top level)
.TP
\fB\-\-on\-conflict\fR \fION_CONFLICT\fR
What to do with items that already exist with other values [possible values: skip, overwrite, keep\-both]
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Import without asking (required without a terminal)
.TP
\fB\-\-identity\-files\fR
Also import the IdentityFiles of an ssh_config as keys
.SS "sverb import known\-hosts"
\fBsverb import known\-hosts\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.PP
Host keys from a known_hosts file (default ~/.ssh/known_hosts)
.TP
\fIPATH\fR
Path to the known_hosts file
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be imported without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fIVAULT\fR
Vault to import into (default: Personal)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
Group to import into (a name or a path like a/b; default: the top level)
.TP
\fB\-\-on\-conflict\fR \fION_CONFLICT\fR
What to do with items that already exist with other values [possible values: skip, overwrite, keep\-both]
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Import without asking (required without a terminal)
.TP
\fB\-\-identity\-files\fR
Also import the IdentityFiles of an ssh_config as keys
.SS "sverb import putty"
\fBsverb import putty\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.PP
Sessions from PuTTY (default ~/.putty/sessions; the registry on Windows)
.TP
\fIPATH\fR
A PuTTY sessions directory (one file per session)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be imported without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fIVAULT\fR
Vault to import into (default: Personal)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
Group to import into (a name or a path like a/b; default: the top level)
.TP
\fB\-\-on\-conflict\fR \fION_CONFLICT\fR
What to do with items that already exist with other values [possible values: skip, overwrite, keep\-both]
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Import without asking (required without a terminal)
.TP
\fB\-\-identity\-files\fR
Also import the IdentityFiles of an ssh_config as keys
.SS "sverb import csv"
\fBsverb import csv\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR
.PP
Hosts from a CSV file (label,address,port,username,group,tags; tags split on ; or |)
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
CSV file
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be imported without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fIVAULT\fR
Vault to import into (default: Personal)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
Group to import into (a name or a path like a/b; default: the top level)
.TP
\fB\-\-on\-conflict\fR \fION_CONFLICT\fR
What to do with items that already exist with other values [possible values: skip, overwrite, keep\-both]
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Import without asking (required without a terminal)
.TP
\fB\-\-identity\-files\fR
Also import the IdentityFiles of an ssh_config as keys
.SS "sverb import backup"
\fBsverb import backup\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR
.PP
A sverb backup
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
Backup file
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be imported without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fIVAULT\fR
Vault to import into (default: Personal)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
Group to import into (a name or a path like a/b; default: the top level)
.TP
\fB\-\-on\-conflict\fR \fION_CONFLICT\fR
What to do with items that already exist with other values [possible values: skip, overwrite, keep\-both]
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Import without asking (required without a terminal)
.TP
\fB\-\-identity\-files\fR
Also import the IdentityFiles of an ssh_config as keys
.SS "sverb export"
\fBsverb export\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR
.PP
Export hosts, backups and recordings
.SS "sverb export backup"
\fBsverb export backup\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR
.PP
Write an encrypted backup of the vault
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
Output file
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an existing file
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-shared\fR
Also include shared vaults (they belong to their organization)
.SS "sverb export ssh\-config"
\fBsverb export ssh\-config\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR
.PP
Write hosts as an OpenSSH config (no secrets)
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
Output file
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an existing file
.SS "sverb export csv"
\fBsverb export csv\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR
.PP
Write hosts as CSV (no secrets)
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
Output file
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an existing file
.SS "sverb export recording"
\fBsverb export recording\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIID\fR \fIOUT\fR
.PP
Export a session recording as asciicast
.TP
\fIID\fR
Recording id (connection id, or the `.cast.sv` file name or path)
.TP
\fIOUT\fR
Output `.cast` file
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the plain\-text confirmation (required without a terminal)
.SS "sverb approve"
\fBsverb approve\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIHOST\fR
.PP
Review and approve locally\-acting fields from sync
.TP
\fIHOST\fR
Label, address or unique fuzzy match
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Approve every listed value with one question
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Approve without asking (scripts; required without a terminal)
.SS "sverb agent"
\fBsverb agent\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Run the built\-in agent exposing forwardable vault keys
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR
Listen on this socket instead of the default in the runtime directory
.SS "sverb lock"
\fBsverb lock\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Lock the vault
.SS "sverb unlock"
\fBsverb unlock\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Unlock the vault
.SS "sverb config"
\fBsverb config\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Check, print or locate config.toml
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Validate config.toml; prints `OK` or `file:line:col: \[u2026]` errors
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-default\fR
Print the default config.toml
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR
Print the path of config.toml
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
With \-\-check: validate this file instead
.SS "sverb doctor"
\fBsverb doctor\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Diagnose terminal capabilities, agent and sync; list SSH algorithms
.TP
\fB\-\-algos\fR
List the supported SSH algorithms
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable output
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR
Mark lines with [ok] [warn] [fail] instead of symbols
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.nf
0  success
1  failure
2  usage error
3  vault locked or unlock failed
4  not found (or ambiguous host)
5  approval required (run `sverb approve <host>`)
6  network or server error
7  partial failure
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBSVERB_HOME\fR
Keep config, data, state and runtime files under this directory (config/, data/, state/, run/) instead of the platform directories.
.TP
\fBSVERB_LOG\fR
Log filter for the log file (default info; for example debug or sverb_conn=trace). RUST_LOG is ignored.
.TP
\fBSVERB_KEYRING\fR
Set to off to never use the OS keyring (the master password is always asked).
.TP
\fBSVERB_EXPORT_PASSWORD\fR
The backup password for export backup and import backup in scripts (instead of a prompt).
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
Any non\-empty value turns colors off; focus and selection use reverse video and bold.
.TP
\fBTERM, LANG, LC_ALL, LC_CTYPE\fR
With ui.ascii = "auto", a non\-UTF\-8 locale or TERM=linux selects ASCII glyphs.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/sverb/config.toml\fR
The configuration (sverb config \-\-path prints the real location; see docs/config.md).
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/sverb/\fR
The encrypted vault database.
.TP
\fI~/.local/state/sverb/\fR
Logs (rotated daily, 7 kept), crash reports and encrypted session recordings.
.PP
On macOS the directories are under ~/Library/Application Support/sverb/, on Windows under %APPDATA%\esverb\e and %LOCALAPPDATA%\esverb\e.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBssh\fR(1), \fBssh_config\fR(5)
.PP
The keybindings, configuration reference, threat model and self\-hosting guide are in the docs/ directory of the source distribution.
